THE CLICK WITHOUT AMPLITUDES: f^T G f against (E f)^2, integer by integer

1. THE IDENTITY (E f)_x^2 + (E f)_y^2 = f^T G f, G = E^T E
  200 random integer vectors of Z^64: identical True
  G symmetric: True; rank 2 (E has two rows); diagonal values [65448, 65501, 65522, 65533, 65536, 65650, 65717, 65773] (256^2 = 65536)
  deviation from 65536 cos(2 pi (j - k) / N): at most 237; entries not circulant (G[j+1][k+1] != G[j][k]): 3696 of 4096
  G kills every antipodal pair e_p + e_(p+32) exactly (C[p+32] = -C[p], S[p+32] = -S[p]): True
  rotation invariance broken by the rounding: e_p^T G e_p differs from 65536 at 60 of 64 phases (the eight values over the births)
  E is not a ring homomorphism on the rounded tables: E(e_1)^2 = (64400, 12750), 256 E(e_2) = (64256, 12800)

